---
description: Splitting a single-mesh supplier GLB (e.g. Jonsered) into articulated groups
globs: public/models/crane/**,src/trw/craneKinematics.ts,scripts/crane/**
---
See src/craneTpl/LESSONS.md L9–L14 and "Rules for splitting a one-mesh model".
- Use connectivity + drawing planes. Put pins on the measured pin-bore rings (concentric circle fits), never invent dimensions, and mark everything else ASSUMED.
- After every split, run the automatic checks: contact islands, posed child/parent contact, def pins vs ring fits (scripts/crane/jonsered/build2.py + samples.py → src/trw/*parts.fixture.json, vitest). Test reach against the drawing table.
- Split cylinders into barrel (parent pin) and rod (child pin).
- Never commit drawings or .trw files.
